From d41d3cbdfb4df05f2f4baaf806c7aeffc118b41a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bare <git@barebrowser.org>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 06:38:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add an incognito toggle to the bottom bar

Restores the fifth bottom bar button. The slot held Ask Gemini until patch 0019
emptied it, which left four buttons and an unbalanced layout. Incognito is a
useful destination that needs no account, and the new tab button remains the
designated centre action, so the original arrangement is unchanged.

The button toggles rather than always opening a new tab: pressing it switches to
the incognito tab model and pressing it again switches back. Switching to an
empty incognito model would show nothing, so a tab is created in that case.

The icon is tinted red while incognito is active. Clearing the tint rather than
setting a colour restores the colour the view already had, so the button matches
its neighbours in any theme. IS_SELECTED is kept in sync as well, since the
default highlight turned out not to be visible on this icon but the state is
still worth being correct.

The tint follows the current tab model rather than only the button press,
because the mode also changes on its own, for instance when the last incognito
tab is closed. TabModelSelectorObserver has no callback for a model switch; the
current model is exposed as an observable supplier instead.

Adding an action to the shared slot needs more than registering it. Both
BottomBarMediator, which decides visibility, and BottomBarView, which maps an
action to a container, hardcoded the two actions that already existed, and each
one silently left the button invisible.

Migration note (8010.27): the mediator now resolves the shared slot once through getCandidateExtraAction(profile, country), caches it, and dispatches per candidate. The incognito answer is given and cached from the renamed method, the upstream body is kept as getCandidateExtraActionUpstream, and the dispatch in updateExtraActionVisibility gains an incognito branch beside the GLIC and AI Mode ones.
